BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20261018T140841Z
UID:a11cb847b167f6db3762e7d7aba4@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular: The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, presente
 d by Citizens\, returns October 1 &#8211\; November 1 with an all-new trai
 l of clever carvings guaranteed to make you smile\, groan\, and laugh out 
 loud. This year’s theme celebrates the art of the pun\, with thousands o
 f hand-carved pumpkins bringing witty wordplay to life through pop culture
  references\, playful characters and pun-believable scenes. From clever on
 e-liners to delightfully cheesy dad jokes\, there’s something to make ev
 ery guest grin as they stroll The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, where over 5\,000 
 glowing jack-o’-lanterns illuminate the Zoo. Don’t miss New England’
 s “must-see” family-friendly event of the Halloween season at Roger Wi
 lliams Park Zoo. All tickets must be purchased online in advance. Tickets 
 are required and sold online only. No refunds or rescheduling. Buy Tickets
 \n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacu
 lar/92071/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue\, Providence\, RI 0
 2907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacular/9207
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bowen’s Wharf Seafood Festival
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTSTAMP:20261018T140841Z
UID:484c2a9c60d0710266c77d9de9f2@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Harvest of the Sea at the 35th Annual Bowen’s 
 Wharf Seafood Festival! Named one of Coastal Living Magazine’s “10 Fab
 ulous Fall Festivals on the Coast\,” this beloved autumn tradition invit
 es everyone to return to the waterfront after the summer rush for two days
  of fresh seafood\, live music\, and family fun. Savor local favorites inc
 luding fish tacos\, lobster rolls\, stuffies\, chowder\, fried calamari\, 
 clams\, oysters\, and more—plus signature cocktails and cold beer beneat
 h Bowen’s Wharf’s colorful tents. Neighboring restaurants and fisherme
 n’s associations serve up their most celebrated seafood dishes\, along w
 ith a few tasty options for landlubbers and kids. Save room for sweet trea
 ts like fresh donuts\, kettle corn and chocolate covered fruit! Bring your
  dancing shoes and enjoy continuous live music throughout the weekend feat
 uring folk\, surf rock and blues bands that are sure to get your toes tapp
 ing. Café-style seating is available throughout the wharf\, and a portion
  of proceeds from the festival bars benefits Child &amp\; Family. Bring th
 e whole family and join locals and visitors alike for this unforgettable w
 aterfront celebration of coastal flavors\, community spirit\, and Newport 
 charm.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/bowen%e2%80%99s-w
 harf-seafood-festival/109514/
LOCATION:Bowen's Wharf\, 13 Bowen's Wharf\, Newport\, RI 02840 Time: 11:00
  AM to 6:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/bowen%e2%80%99s-wharf-seafood-f
 estival/109514/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Kaleidoscope" Performance at Newport Elks Lodge
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261018T140841Z
UID:97ce1866aa0f01342b66914dea83@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:"Kaleidoscope" Performance by Newport Contemporary Ballet at E
 lks Lodge in Newport When: Friday\, October 16th at 7:00 PM Saturday\, Oct
 ober 17th at 7:00 PM Sunday\, October 18th at 2:00 PM Where: Newport Elks 
 Lodge\, 141 Pelham Street\, Newport Kaleidoscope is an ever-evolving mosai
 c of dance and emotion. As we bring our focus to the stage\, the world shi
 fts and expands before our eyes. Each work acts as a unique shard of glass
  that is vibrant\, distinct\, and beautiful on its own and then comes toge
 ther with the others to form a beautifully intricate masterpiece. Opening 
 our 45th Season\, Kaleidoscope features world premiere works by internatio
 nally renowned choreographer\, Katarzyna Skarpetowska\, former NCB dancer
 \, Lauren Difede\, and Artistic &amp\; Executive Director\, Danielle Genes
 t. NCB’s Rehearsal Director\, Emily Baker’s powerful piece Shattered G
 lass will round out this fascinating program by a phenomenal group of fema
 le choreographers. There will be a short moderated “Talk Back” followi
 ng the opening night performance of Kaleidoscope.\n\nSource: https://www.v
 isitrhodeisland.com/event/kaleidoscope-performance-at-newport-elks-lodge/1
 11845/
LOCATION:Elks Lodge\, 141 Pelham Street\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/kaleidoscope-performance-at-new
 port-elks-lodge/111845/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4th Annual Garlic and Apple Roast
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261018T140841Z
UID:f8013f65a2aa1b96ac9a1e27d15a@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:4th Annual Garlic and Apple Roast When: Sunday\, October 18th 
 from 10:00 AM to 2:00 PM Where: Tiverton Middle School\, 10 Quintal Drive
 \, Tiverton\, R.I. Join us on Sunday October 18th\, 2026 from 10:00 AM to 
 2:00 PM for our 4th Annual Garlic &amp\; Apple Roast. Garlic might be scar
 ce this season\, so we are adding in the beloved apple. Let’s celebrate 
 the season's harvest! Vendors will be Infusing garlic and apples into uniq
 ue food &amp\; dishes and sharing them with you. Get out\, socialize and t
 ry something new and delicious. More details to come. Event will be moving
  INSIDE this year at the Tiverton Middle School Cafeteria\, located at 10 
 Quintal Drive\, Tiverton\, RI 02878. Sponsored by The Bay Magazine. Event 
 is free and open to the public. Location: Tiverton Middle School Cafeteria
 \, 10 Quintal Drive\, Tiverton\, RI 02878. Hours: 10am - 2pm.\n\nSource: h
 ttps://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/4th-annual-garlic-and-apple-roast/11
 1795/
LOCATION:Tiverton Middle School Cafeteria\, 10 Quintal Drive\, Tiverton\, 
 RI 02878. Hours: 10am - 2pm. Show More View Website | Email 1 / 1 Addition
 al Information\, 10 Quintal Drive\, Tiverton Middle School\, Tiverton\, RI
  02878
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/4th-annual-garlic-and-apple-roa
 st/111795/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261018T140841Z
UID:045d082951d5ecc2b958cb870f3d@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
